205→
206→Finds the nearest point from input 1 and transfers its color to create a Voronoi pattern.
207→
208→### Distance-based Color Transfer
209→
210→```vex
211→int pt = nearpoint(1, @P);
212→vector pos = point(1, 'P', pt);
213→vector col = point(1, 'Cd', pt);
214→float d = distance(@P, pos);
215→d = fit(d, 0, ch('radius'), 1, 0);
216→d = clamp(d, 0, 1);
217→@Cd = col * d;
218→```
219→
220→Finds the nearest point on a second input geometry, retrieves its position and color, then calculates the distance from the current point to that nearest point.
221→
222→### Distance-based color falloff
223→
224→```vex
225→int pt = nearpoints(1, @P, 1)[0];
226→vector pos = point(1, 'P', pt);
227→vector col = point(1, 'Cd', pt);
228→float d = distance(@P, pos);
229→d = fit(d, 0, ch('radius'), 1, 0);
230→d = clamp(d, 0, 1);
231→@Cd = col * d;
232→```
233→
234→Calculates the distance from each point to its nearest neighbor on a second input, then uses fit() and clamp() to create a distance-based falloff value that modulates the color transfer.
235→
236→### Distance-based color transfer with fit
237→
238→```vex
239→int pt = nearpoint(1, v@P);
240→vector pos = point(1, "P", pt);
241→vector col = point(1, "Cd", pt);
242→float d = distance(pos, v@P);
243→v@Cd = fit(d, 0, chf("radius"), col, v@Cd);
244→```
245→
246→Finds the nearest point on input 1, calculates the distance to it, then uses fit() to blend between the nearest point's color and the current point's color based on distance within a controllable r....
247→
248→### Multi-Point Blending with nearpoints
249→
250→```vex
251→int pt = nearpoint(1, @P);
252→vector pos = point(1, "P", pt);
253→vector col = point(1, "Cd", pt);
254→float d = distance(@P, pos);
255→d = fit(d, 0, ch("radius"), 1, 0);
256→d = clamp(d, 0, 1);
257→@Cd = col * d;
258→
259→// ...
260→```
261→
262→Demonstrates the limitation of using nearpoint() for color blending, where values cannot blend across Voronoi cell boundaries.
263→
264→### Expanding nearpoints search radius
265→
266→```vex
267→int pts[] = nearpoints(1, @P, 10);
268→int pt = pts[0];
269→vector pos = point(1, "P", pt);
270→vector col = point(1, "Cd", pt);
271→float d = distance(@P, pos);
272→d = fit(d, 0, ch("radius"), 0, 1.0);
273→d = clamp(d, 0, 1);
274→@Cd = col * d;
275→```
276→
277→Modifies the nearpoints function to search within a specified distance (10 units) rather than finding just the closest point, allowing for blending across cell boundaries.
